$add_soft_subtitles — burn soft subtitles from texts[] onto videos[]

SUMMARY
  For each videos[] clip, burns subtitles from texts[].
  .ass / .ssa / .srt files in texts[] (e.g. from $file(..., source_path=True)) use ffmpeg
  subtitles=; inline ASS text or [Script Info] also uses subtitles=; plain text uses drawtext=.

SYNTAX
  $add_soft_subtitles
  $add_soft_subtitles(font='ttf/MuseoSansCyrl-700.ttf', size=40, bottom=40)
  $add_soft_subtitles(text='Fixed caption for all clips')

INPUT
  videos[] — required
  texts[]  — subtitle strings (one per video, one for all, or pad with last entry)

OUTPUT
  videos[] — one MP4 per input video (only videos[] in the output bundle)

PAIRING
  Equal counts — zip video[i] with texts[i]
  One texts[] entry — same subtitles on every video
  Fewer texts than videos — pad with the last text entry
  More texts than videos — use the first N texts

ARGUMENTS
  text=   — fixed subtitle for every video (overrides texts[])
  font=   — .ttf path (default: ttf/MuseoSansCyrl-700.ttf under repo root)
  size=   — font size in pixels (default: 40)
  bottom= — margin from bottom edge in pixels (default: 40)

TEXT RULES
  If len(text) > 10, caret ^ in text is replaced with newline.

DEPENDENCIES
  ffmpeg + ffprobe: uv run python tools/download_ffmpeg.py  (→ tools/ffmpeg/)
  or system install on PATH

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_ADD_SOFT_SUBTITLES=1 — stub .mp4 links without ffmpeg

EXAMPLE
  @clip: $file('clip.mp4')
  @lines: $list('Hello^World')
  @titled: (@clip, @lines) -> $add_soft_subtitles -> $save('clip_subs.mp4')

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No — output is videos[] only (texts[] and other arrays cleared).
